{
  "_note": [
    "States, provinces and regions outside the US, and the starter cities that sit under them.",
    "US states live in geo.json — they are complete, so every US city has one.",
    "This file is deliberately not complete. A region is listed only when a city in",
    "cities.json belongs to it, so every region page has something on it. Adding a",
    "region here with no city under it would ship an empty page, which is worse for",
    "search than no page at all.",
    "",
    "A region is also left out when it would carry the same slug as the only city in it.",
    "Berlin, Tokyo, Dubai and Madrid gain nothing from /de/berlin/berlin, so those cities",
    "keep the short path and no region row is created. Routing handles both shapes in the",
    "same country — see app/lib/geo.php.",
    "",
    "code is what gets printed after a city name (\"Toronto, ON\"). Left null where the",
    "country has no short form people would recognise; the full name is used instead.",
    "City names must match cities.json exactly."
  ],
